<newsitem itemid="150031" id="root" date="1996-10-29" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Datatec half-year earnings jump.</title>
<headline>Datatec half-year earnings jump.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-year ended August 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr per combined unit (cts)  20.9 vs 11.7</p>
<p>    - attrib EPS		     16.0 vs 7.2</p>
<p>    - debenture interest	   4.9  vs 4.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			   -   vs  -</p>
<p>    Attrib income		    4.13 vs 1.44</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			    5.83 vs 2.27</p>
<p>    Tax				  2.22 vs 0.94</p>
<p>    Turnover			 170.25 vs 25.31</p>
<p>Full name: Datatec Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Softare firm Datatex that it was not paying a dividend in view of the size of the interest distribution relative to earnings per combined unit.</p>
<p>Turnover and profits were boosted by a series of acquisitions in the period. The company said it was now in a position where, for the first time, hard currency earnings will contribute a meaningful percentage of net income.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
